# installer-guard source-ready SHA-256 receipt; excludes this receipt.
# SOURCE ONLY: compiler, Clippy, tests, native API, MSI pairing and installer lifecycle NOT RUN in this lease.
# R3 P2 cause: individually mapped RVA descriptor rows could alternate low/far physical offsets and replay the stream.
# Repair: one checked PhysicalRange/rva_range admits each COMPLETE normal/delay descriptor directory before RVA metadata I/O.
# Shared admission also covers complete export directory, EAT, export name-pointer and ordinal arrays; physical row walks never remap.
# file_range bounds complete optional header and section table. Partial overlapping mappings fail closed before table iteration.
# Dynamic names retain single-physical-section bounds and overlap cache; thunk/IAT tables are not traversed.
# No whole-image buffering, architecture expansion, cap weakening, dependency change or exported ABI change.
# Four new file-backed test functions: alternating 94-section normal/delay descriptors, normal/delay boundaries, all export table boundaries, partial overlap.
# Alternating case has 92 valid distinct names plus null descriptor; two-window test read ceiling; expected one 64 KiB read and zero rewinds.
# Boundary oracles accept exact section end and refuse one-byte crossing before far reads.
# Existing 32 portable tests and Windows ignored database pairing test preserved; now 36 portable plus one Windows ignored test authored, NOT RUN.
# Formatter: pinned rustfmt 1.99.1, PID 44172, 10-second timeout, exit 0; only src/pe.rs and tests/stream.rs formatted.
